  "title": "Factorial of a given number",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "contentStatus": "plus",
  "levelType": "practical",
  "statementHtml": "<p>You are given an integer <strong>n</strong>. Return the value of <strong>n!</strong> or <strong>n factorial</strong>.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Factorial </strong>of a number is the <strong>product </strong>of <strong>all </strong>positive integers less than or equal to that number.</p>",
  "examples": [
    "<p><strong>Input</strong>: n = 2</p><p><strong>Output</strong>: 2</p><p><strong>Explanation</strong>: 2! = 1 * 2 = 2.</p>",
    "<p><strong>Input</strong>: n = 0</p><p><strong>Output</strong>: 1</p><p><strong>Explanation</strong>: 0! is defined as 1.</p>",
    "<p>Input: 3</p>"
  ],
  "constraintsHtml": "<ul><li>0 <= n <= 10</li></ul>",
